meta {
  name: Enroll Application Course
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/applications/courses/{{applicationCourseId}}/enroll
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("enrollmentId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Final step of the admission pipeline — token_paid -> enrolled. Creates the
  Enrollment record (the real student<->college link — see docs/context.md
  §11 "Post-Admission") and flips the ApplicationCourse's status to
  "enrolled". Requires staff_member auth, no special permission code.

  409 ConflictError "This course's token must be paid before enrolling" if
  the course isn't at "token_paid" yet. 409 ConflictError "No seats
  available for this quota" if the course's chosen quota seat pool is
  exhausted at the moment of enrolling (seat is decremented here, not
  earlier in the pipeline).

  Idempotent — re-calling this on an already-enrolled course just returns
  the existing Enrollment, does not re-issue or double-decrement a seat.

  404 if the course doesn't exist or belongs to a different college.
}
